comment 2026-11-11T12:00:00Z
    Prior art: the P3 and P4 cards before the interleave (the user, 2026-11-11). Superseded by the area cards
    (P3, P4, P11 to P15); general content moved to them (speed targets and coverage record to P15).

    P3 card:

    > **Class:** not readily verifiable.
    >
    > **Kind:** verification-suite.
    >
    > **Goal:** a new, clean conformance suite at production quality in
    > `packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/`, running against the prototype runtime (round 14) and,
    > from P4, the production runtime, through one Port; one oracle per guarantee with its mutants;
    > the old suite's fixtures, scenarios, reference model and lies copied, its runner, lock, shims
    > and text formats rewritten.
    >
    > **Verified by:**
    >
    > - the new suite green on round 14 with the old suite's verdicts;
    > - null 0 of N;
    > - falsify (every oracle kills its mutants, each for the expected reason);
    > - an audit and re-audit by a lead that did not build it (skill:policy-testing#audit-a-suite);
    > - its coverage record, in @plan.Runtime's verification once the user says yes to that Plan edit.
    >
    > **One iteration:** one Task: grow the suite from its Spec, run it on round 14 and the null
    > runtime, run its mutants, get the hourly review, gather findings by root cause.
    >
    > **Exit criteria:**
    >
    > - the suite passes on round 14;
    > - it kills every mutant the old suite kills;
    > - every oracle kills its own mutants;
    > - it passes its audit and re-audit;
    > - its fast gates run in `nub run verify`;
    > - its coverage record exists;
    > - the user's speed targets hold (Q4 A, 2026-11-08):
    >   - the suite in one process at most 15 s,
    >   - peak RSS per suite process at most 600 MB,
    >   - the builder's fast loop at most 30 s wall,
    >   - every final-commit gate at up to 8 in parallel at most 10 min wall,
    >   - or the gap reported with its limiter.
    >
    > **False pass:** agreeing with the old suite because it was copied, weaknesses included.
    >
    > **Caught by:** the audit on the new suite, whose auditor writes its own mutants from the Specs.
    >
    > **Gates:**
    >
    > - falsify, which rejects the null runtime and every registered mutant
    >   (`packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/`, each oracle's mutants file);
    > - `nub run check`, which rejects a planted lint violation.
    >
    > **Failure limit:** 2.
    >
    > **Stops:**
    >
    > - a guarantee change (a Spec Invariant added, dropped or changed);
    > - a guarantee that can't be met.
    >
    > **User's read:**
    >
    > - the suite layout (decided in round 1),
    > - each Spec revision,
    > - each changed expected result with its reason.
    >
    > **Draws from:**
    >
    > - skill:policy-verification (prove a suite; the coverage record);
    > - skill:policy-testing (audit a suite; scenarios that enforce each Invariant written first);
    > - skill:to-spec for the suite's own Spec;
    > - skill:policy-convergence at the threshold;
    > - skill:review for the hourly reviews;
    > - skill:check-benchmark on the speed numbers.

    P4 card:

    > **Class:** verifiable.
    >
    > **Kind:** feature.
    >
    > **Goal:** the production runtime for what the prototypes proved, in
    > `packages/flow-state-v3/src/`, built from the core Specs with the prototype open beside it, one
    > module at a time: Compiled and the compiler; lane, step and turn; the persistence edge,
    > write-ahead and the driver; restore and key versions; fragments; operations; the CLI's `check`,
    > `explain` and `graph`.
    >
    > **Starts when:** interleaved with P3 by area (the Epic's instructions): each module starts once
    > its area's suite is proven and audited; T15's cross-area audit gates T23.
    >
    > **Verified by:**
    >
    > - P3's suite through a production adapter (coverage record in @plan.Runtime);
    > - skill:check-task per Task;
    > - `nub run check` at zero;
    > - `nub run verify`.
    >
    > **One iteration:** the next ready Task: build it against its Spec, check it independently,
    > repair. The Pay path first, end to end, as the walking skeleton.
    >
    > **Exit criteria:**
    >
    > - the suite passes on the production runtime alone, the prototype adapter retired;
    > - every gate fails on its broken runtime;
    > - `nub run verify` passes;
    > - the completion audit passes.
    >
    > **False pass:** the production adapter doing work the runtime should.
    >
    > **Caught by:** mutants run against the production adapter, and a review section on the adapter's
    > role.
    >
    > **Gates:**
    >
    > - falsify on the production adapter;
    > - one probe file per lint rule that `nub run check` must reject (`tools/lint-bomb/`).
    >
    > **Failure limit:** 2.
    >
    > **Stops:**
    >
    > - public entry-point names;
    > - a large public API change;
    > - a guarantee that can't be met;
    > - a guarantee change.
    >
    > **User's read:** the internal module layout; small public API calls.
    >
    > **Draws from:**
    >
    > - skill:policy-testing: test first, module integration tests through the public interface (no
    >   unit tests of internals), and the scenarios that enforce each Invariant written before the code;
    > - skill:playbook-build (long runs);
    > - skill:execute-task;
    > - skill:check-task;
    > - skill:to-design per module;
    > - skill:review;
    > - skill:diagnose when a case fails unexplained.
